  "reasoning": "B appeared before the German court, argued the merits, and was informed in writing of the right to contest jurisdiction and the consequences of appearing. Under Article 26(2), the required protection for a weaker party is therefore satisfied, and Article 26(1) confers jurisdiction by appearance. The protective consumer rule would ordinarily require A to sue B only in the courts of France under Article 18(2), assuming the consumer-contract scope in Article 17(1)(c) is met, but it does not prevent jurisdiction based on B's valid appearance.",
